From 76b74f9b168e4aff6f2997b7e7141ce1c0531a1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Steven Barrett <steven@liquorix.net>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:30:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mm/mglru: Sync the MGLRU-FG backport with v5 of the series

This branch carries v4 of the MGLRU-FG series on v7.3.  The author
posted v5 for mm-new.  v5 does not apply to v7.3, so this commit takes
the changes that v5 made to v4 and that do not need mm-new.

Kairui Song lists these changes in the cover letter of v5:

  - Code and design are basically the same, mostly rebase and
    adaption and comment updates.
  - Pick up two patches from Ridong Chen to avoid conflicts.
  - Share the ancestor walk between lruvec_live_lock_irq() and the
    new folio_lruvec_live_get()

The first patch from Ridong Chen is "mm/mglru: rename the generation
offset in lru_gen_folio_seq()":

  lru_gen_folio_seq() computes how many generations below max_seq a
  folio should be added to, but stores it in a variable named "gen".
  Elsewhere in MGLRU "gen" means an index into lrugen->folios[], i.e.
  seq % MAX_NR_GENS, so reusing the name for a relative offset is
  confusing.

  Rename it to "age", which matches what the value means: the newest
  generation is age 1, and a larger age is an older generation.

  No functional change.

The second patch is "mm/mglru: skip the flags cmpxchg when nothing
changes":

  folio_update_gen() and folio_set_lru_refs() always end with a
  try_cmpxchg() on folio->flags, even when the new value equals the
  old one. The locked instruction still takes the struct page
  cacheline in exclusive state.

  [...]

  Break out of the loop when the flags would not change. The update
  is complete at the point of that read: the flags already hold the
  target value, and a concurrent change to them is ordered after it.
  When the cmpxchg would have succeeded, the value written is the
  same, so no new state becomes reachable.

  [...]

  [kasong: folio_update_gen() is replaced by folio_inc_lru_refs_walk()
  later in the series, which keeps the same early exit.]

